Date: 2026-10-03   Session: ops-b   Items: OPS-21, OPS-22 (both close)

Read-only throughout. No package installed, promoted, deployed or restarted.

1. WHAT WAS WRONG (OPS-21)
   docs/software-status.md `Installed` column derived its date from the mtime of
   /var/lib/dpkg/info/<pkg>.list. dpkg rewrites that file on every unpack, so the
   column reported the LAST UPGRADE date under the heading "Installed".

2. FIX
   New scripts/build-update/apt_history.py parses /var/log/apt/history.log plus its
   rotated .gz siblings, which record Start-Date, the exact Commandline and separate
   Install: / Upgrade: / Remove: / Purge: lines.

   $ python3 scripts/build-update/apt_history.py
   packages indexed      : 4445
     installed           : 4281
     upgrade-only (pre-window): 86
     installed unattended: 2098
   log files read        : ['history.log.1.gz', 'history.log.2.gz', 'history.log']

   Note: §19 OPS-21 says the log "holds 13 dated transactions". Measured, it holds
   186 across the three files; 13 is the live history.log alone.

   $ python3 -c "...pl.apt_date(...)..."
   nginx              not installed (removed/purged 2026-08-23)
   dbeaver-ce         not installed (removed/purged 2026-10-01)
   rclone             2026-10-03 (apt history, Install)
   foxglove-studio    2026-10-01 (apt history, Install)
   bash               2026-04-23 (dpkg mtime)

   Cross-checked against the raw log:
   $ sed -n '72,77p' /var/log/apt/history.log
   Start-Date: 2026-10-03 08:21:06
   Commandline: /usr/bin/apt-get install -y -qq rclone
   Install: rclone:amd64 (1.60.1+dfsg-4ubuntu3.2)

3. SILENT FAILURE FOUND AND FIXED
   The first integration used `import apt_history`, which resolves against sys.path
   (whose [0] is the CWD). refresh-install-log.sh does `cd "$AO_ROOT"` first, so the
   import raised ImportError on EVERY production run and silently fell back to the
   dpkg mtime — the exact source being replaced. Output looked normal. Now loaded by
   __file__; asserted by test_apt_history_loads_regardless_of_working_directory.

4. DEFECT FOUND BY THE NEW TESTS (OPS-22)
   update_steps() accepted a digest on the "sha256:" prefix alone. `sha256:` + 12
   hex chars passed, emitting `podman pull repo@sha256:<12>` — HTTP 400 from any
   registry. is_complete_digest() now checks algorithm AND body length.

   $ python3 scripts/build-update/test_generators.py
   Ran 29 tests in 0.282s
   OK

   The suite did not run at all beforehand: a stray fragment hung off EOF after
   unittest.main() (dead code), and TestAptHistoryParsing called importlib.reload()
   on a module never in sys.modules. Parser now takes an injectable log_dir so tests
   use tempfile.mkdtemp() and never touch /var/log/apt.

